    bottomLine: "The best screen here for watching your own streaming services, with no membership required.",
    description: "The T16 has a 22 by 60-inch deck, 0 to 15% incline with no decline, 0.5 to 12 mph and a 375 lb maximum user weight. Its 16-inch HD touchscreen runs JRNY plus Netflix, Prime Video, YouTube, Spotify and a web browser over Wi-Fi, so streaming uses your existing accounts rather than a treadmill membership, and Bowflex says the treadmill works without a JRNY subscription. It also pairs over Bluetooth FTMS with Zwift and Peloton’s app on another device. Bowflex rates the motor at 3.5 HP under test settings, a figure we keep off the spec line because it is not a continuous rating. The US warranty is lifetime on the frame and motor, three years on parts and one year of labour. Bowflex listed it at $1,999 against $2,299 on 5 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "nordictrack-commercial-1750",
