        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>What is the best treadmill with a screen?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It depends on what you want the screen for. For iFIT classes on a budget, the NordicTrack T Series 10; for a screen with no membership at all, the Sole F80; for streaming your own apps, the Bowflex T16; for running-focused iFIT with decline, the NordicTrack Commercial 1750; and for the biggest screen and Peloton classes, the Peloton Tread Vision. We have not tested them.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you use a treadmill with a screen without a subscription?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes, on all six here, but how much of the screen works varies. NordicTrack runs in manual mode, Peloton’s Just Run sets speed and incline manually, Echelon runs manually with a free account according to reviews, the Bowflex T16 runs programs and streaming apps, and the Sole F80 needs no membership for anything.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How big is the NordicTrack T Series 10 touchscreen?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The current T Series 10 (NTL15425) has a 10-inch touchscreen that tilts. NordicTrack covers the screen for one year. Older models sold under similar names have had different consoles, so check the model number.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Which treadmill has the biggest screen?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Of the six here, the Peloton Tread Vision, at 23.8 inches. NordicTrack’s Commercial 2450 and X24 have 24-inch screens, and Peloton’s Tread+ Vision also has a 23.8-inch screen, at higher prices.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you watch Netflix on a treadmill screen?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On some. The Bowflex T16 runs Netflix, Prime Video and YouTube with your own accounts. Current touchscreen NordicTracks offer Netflix through iFIT on its top plan. Peloton and Echelon screens are built around their own classes. With any treadmill, a tablet on a holder will play whatever you like.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is a built-in screen better than using a tablet?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              A built-in screen can let a trainer change the speed and incline for you and needs no setup. A tablet is cheaper, runs any app, and is easy to replace, but usually cannot control the treadmill. If you want classes that drive the machine, buy the built-in screen; if you just want something to watch, use a tablet.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
          <div class="author-card">
